---
import MissionLayout from '../../layouts/MissionLayout.astro';
---

<MissionLayout
  slug="zippyzack"
  heading="ZippyZack.com"
  status="Storefront sneak peek"
  statusHref="https://www.zippyzack.com/storefront"
  heroImage="/assets/projects/zippyzack-hero.webp"
  explorerGradient="linear-gradient(40deg, #005247 0%, #007f5f 100%)"
>
  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">1. The TL;DR <span class="case-section-sub">(Executive Summary)</span></h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">The Purpose</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Help crocheters get from a project idea to a ready-to-make kit.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">The Problem</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Choosing a crochet project is only part of the work: makers also need to identify the right yarn, tools, and quantities. ZippyZack groups project-specific supplies together and lets shoppers leave out tools they already own, while making clear whether they are buying materials or a completed piece.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">The Solution</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">A multi-page storefront with project and difficulty discovery, itemized kit details, optional-tool pricing, a basket, payment and order-support information, plus a separate gallery of finished crochet work.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">2. Strategy &amp; Discovery</h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Audience &amp; Discovery</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">The shop speaks to people who are new to crochet as well as experienced makers looking for their next project. Visitors can browse by difficulty (Beginner, Easy, Intermediate, or Advanced), search makes, or start with a project idea rather than sourcing supplies separately.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Kit Promise</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">A kit brings the listed yarn and tools for a specific make together in one box. Product pages separate the kit from a finished item and credit the original designer.</p>
    </div>
    
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">3. Execution <span class="case-section-sub">(The &ldquo;How&rdquo;)</span></h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Storefront &amp; Navigation</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">The storefront leads with project-ready kits, then points visitors to bundles, makes, and a gallery. The home page also features popular projects, difficulty-based entry points, a short maker introduction, and a newsletter sign-up.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Make Detail &amp; Pricing</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">A make page can show skill level, estimated time, kit contents, quantities, and item prices. Shoppers can untick eligible tools they already own and see the kit total update.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Live Experience</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value"><a class="case-link" href="https://www.zippyzack.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit the launch page ↗</a> · <a class="case-link" href="https://www.zippyzack.com/storefront" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the storefront sneak peek ↗</a> · <a class="case-link" href="https://www.zippyzack.com/makes" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Browse makes ↗</a> · <a class="case-link" href="https://www.zippyzack.com/gallery" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View the gallery ↗</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Visual Highlights</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Screenshots captured from the live site in November 2026. Browse the storefront, kit detail, finished-piece gallery, contact, order tracking, shipping and returns, and care instructions. There is no standalone FAQ page at the live /faq route; common customer questions are covered across the support pages.</p>
      <div class="gallery-wrap">
        <div class="gallery-track-wrap">
          <div class="gallery-track">
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/zippyzack-storefront.png" alt="ZippyZack storefront landing page with project-ready kit messaging and browse links" />
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/zippyzack-make-detail.png" alt="A cute beanie make page showing difficulty, estimated time, four kit items, and optional tools" />
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/zippyzack-gallery.png" alt="ZippyZack finished crochet gallery featuring a beanie, daisy top, and floral bucket hat" />
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/zippyzack-contact.png" alt="ZippyZack contact page with workshop information, phone, and email details" />
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/zippyzack-order-tracking.png" alt="ZippyZack order tracking page with order number and email lookup form" />
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/zippyzack-shipping-returns.png" alt="ZippyZack shipping and returns page with shipping costs and delivery-time information" />
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/zippyzack-care.png" alt="ZippyZack care instructions page covering washing, blocking, and storage of crochet pieces" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="gallery-controls">
          <button class="gallery-btn" aria-label="Previous screenshot">&#8592; Back</button>
          <span class="gallery-counter">1 / 7</span>
          <button class="gallery-btn" aria-label="Next screenshot">Next &#8594;</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</MissionLayout>
